<title>USA: St Paul hogs off $.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Paul hogs off $.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts were $.50 lower</p>
<p>in slow trade. Top $56.00 per cwt. - USDA</p>
<p>US 1-3    220-250 lbs     56.00</p>
<p>	    250-260 lbs     55.50-56.00</p>
<p>	    260-270 lbs     54.50-55.50</p>
<p>US 2-3    270-280 lbs     53.50-54.50</p>
<p>US 2-4    280-290 lbs     52.50-53.50</p>
<p>US 3-4    290-300 lbs     51.50-52.50</p>
<p>Sows under 500 lbs .50/1.50 higher; 500-700 lbs 1.00/2.50 higher. Top 51.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3    300-400 lbs     45.50-47.00</p>
<p>	    400-500 lbs     47.00-48.00</p>
<p>	    500-550 lbs     49.00-49.50</p>
<p>	    550-700 lbs     50.00-51.00</p>
</text>
